color{blue}4}$ and an argument of ${\\color{red}9}.$ Therefore, we can combine them by adding their coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{log}_{4}⁡(9)-3{log}_{3}⁡(9)+5{log}_{4}⁡(9) & =(2+5){log}_{4}⁡(9)-3{log}_{3}⁡(9) \\\\  & =7{log}_{4}⁡(9)-3{log}_{3}⁡(9)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115027 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4007" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115027 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $9\\log_6(2x)-2\\log_4(2x)-3\\log_4(2x).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115027 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c45b5963-9e06-558c-b125-f8202e42b1af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115027 #edb/ref 1074 "Both the second and the third logarithmic terms have a base of ${\\color{blue}4}$ and an argument of ${\\color{red}2x}.$ Therefore, we can combine them by adding their coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{log}_{6}⁡(2x)-2{log}_{4}⁡(2x)-3{log}_{4}⁡(2x) & =9{log}_{6}⁡(2x)+(-2-3){log}_{4}⁡(2x) \\\\  & =9{log}_{6}⁡(2x)-5{log}_{4}⁡(2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115196 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049589 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115196 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050469 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115196 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115578 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115196 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115581 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115196 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186526096 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115196 #edb/ref 1039 "Simplifying Logarithmic Expressions Containing Two Terms" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115196 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186115025 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115196 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "1446af0e-7200-51cf-942d-9db92e9ae721" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115197 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115579 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115197 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115931 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115197 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186526010 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115197 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186526031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921861151