045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526030 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is equivalent to $7\\operatorname{log}⁡(5x)-2\\operatorname{log}⁡(5x)+5\\operatorname{log}⁡(3x)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526030 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "68542d18-8a32-5e4e-8371-82abbbeca5f9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526030 #edb/ref 1074 "Both the first and the second logarithmic terms have a base of $10$ and an argument of $5x.$ Therefore, we can combine them by adding their coefficients.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7\\operatorname{log}⁡(5x)-2\\operatorname{log}⁡(5x)+5\\operatorname{log}⁡(3x) & =(7-2)\\operatorname{log}⁡(5x)+5\\operatorname{log}⁡(3x) \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{log}⁡(5x)+5\\operatorname{log}⁡(3x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526031 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186525956 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526031 #edb/ref 1069 "q-24170" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526031 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526031 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is equivalent to $\\operatorname{log}⁡(6)-3\\operatorname{log}⁡(4)+3\\operatorname{log}⁡(6)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526031 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "68b55bab-dfd4-5ef5-a0ec-17580bbcfd66" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526031 #edb/ref 1074 "Both the first and the third logarithmic terms have a base of $10$ and an argument of $6.$ Therefore, we can combine them by adding their coefficients.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{log}⁡(6)-3\\operatorname{log}⁡(4)+3\\operatorname{log}⁡(6) & =(1+3)\\operatorname{log}⁡(6)-3\\operatorname{log}⁡(4) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{log}⁡(6)-3\\operatorname{log}⁡(4)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526096 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186525946 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526096 #edb/ref 1069 "q-66634" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526096 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526096 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is equivalent to $7{log}_{